<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>First Party Data marketing stays off; transactional only</td><td>Without first party data consent proof, marketing has no legal footing</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>First first party data touches teach and reassure before selling</td><td>First Party Data margin suffers when discounts arrive first</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Context-rich first party data nudge before any incentive</td><td>Margin-safe first party data recovery at peak intent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Pause first party data promos; switch to post-purchase teaching</td><td>Keeps first party data buyers from instant list fatigue</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>First Party Data selling waits for case resolution</td><td>First Party Data messaging lands badly during open cases</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Remove chronic first party data non-openers pre-complaint</td><td>Shields first party data sender reputation and inboxing</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Hold first party data texts to quiet hours and frequency limits</td><td>First Party Data SMS risk exceeds email per complaint</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Send first party data B2B accounts down their own track</td><td>First Party Data retail promos can violate B2B terms</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>First Party Data automation skips unverified domains first</td><td>Unverified first party data addresses poison sender score</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Strip first party data test data from live journeys</td><td>QA first party data sends distort real performance</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Treat first party data snoops under normal consent policy</td><td>Manual first party data exceptions rot the audit trail</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Re-permission legacy first party data lists pre-automation</td><td>Timestamp-less first party data consent is legal exposure</td></tr>
